VALUES (
  'issue-001-claude-opus-5-and-what-it-means-for-you',
  'Issue #1 — Claude Opus 5 is absurdly good, and here''s what that actually means',
  'Honest first impressions of Claude Opus 5, three AI workflows worth stealing, what everyone gets wrong about "AI privacy," and why we built Aethyro the way we did.',
  E'# Welcome to The Aethyro Dispatch 👋\n\n*Issue #1 · September 2026*\n\nHey. Welcome to the first Dispatch.\n\nI''m going to keep this simple: no corporate newsletter energy, no 47-step frameworks you''ll never use, no affiliate links. Just what''s real, what''s working, and what''s complete nonsense dressed up in a press release.\n\nEvery issue is going to be short, direct, and actually useful. If it''s not, tell me.\n\nLet''s go.\n\n---\n\n## 🔥 The Big Thing: Claude Opus 5\n\nAnthropic shipped Claude Opus 5 this year, and I want to be honest with you about it — because the hype makes it hard to know what''s actually true.\n\n**It''s genuinely the best model right now.** Not "best for price" or "best for certain tasks." Just best. We''ve been running it since launch and the gap vs. GPT-4o on complex reasoning and long document work is real. It''s not marketing.\n\nHere''s what impressed us most:\n\n- **Long document understanding.** We threw a 120-page contract at it and asked for a risk summary with clause citations. The citations were accurate. GPT-4o hallucinated two.\n- **Code quality.** Not just "it writes code" — it writes code that actually runs, catches edge cases, and explains its own reasoning when you ask it to.\n- **Honesty about limits.** When it doesn''t know something, it says so. That matters more than people realize.\n\n**The catch?** It''s expensive to run directly through the API. That''s why Aethyro exists — we handle the API, you get Opus 5, and you pay credit packs instead of a monthly subscription that charges you even when you don''t use it.\n\n---\n\n## 💡 3 Workflows Worth Stealing This Week\n\n**1. The "rubber duck" planning session**\n\nBefore you start any project, open Aethyro and just... talk through it. Tell it what you''re trying to do, what you''re unsure about, what the constraints are. You''re not asking it to plan the project — you''re using it as a sounding board.\n\nThe act of explaining it to Claude forces you to notice the gaps in your own thinking. Every time.\n\nTry: *"I''m planning to launch a new service offering next month. Here''s my rough idea: [describe it]. What am I not thinking about?"*\n\n**2. The contract speed-read**\n\nAnytime you get a contract, NDA, or terms doc, paste it in and ask:\n\n*"Identify the top 3 risks for me as the [buyer/vendor/employee] and flag any unusual or one-sided clauses."*\n\nYou still need a lawyer for anything that matters. But this tells you what to look for and what to ask before you pay legal fees.\n\n**3. The "explain this to a 12-year-old" trick**\n\nIf you''re struggling to understand something technical — a financial statement, a piece of code, a legal clause — ask Claude to explain it at a 12-year-old level. Then ask it to add the nuance back. This two-step approach works better than asking for a "simple explanation" because it forces the model to actually strip away jargon first.\n\n---\n\n## 🤔 Real Talk: What "AI Privacy" Actually Means\n\nEveryone says their AI product is "private." Here''s what to actually look for:\n\n**Training on your data** — The big one. Does the provider use your conversations to train future models? OpenAI does this by default (you can opt out). Anthropic does NOT train on API inputs. When you chat in Aethyro, your messages go to Anthropic''s API and come right back. They''re not in a training set.\n\n**Data retention** — How long does the provider keep your messages? This is separate from training. Check the privacy policy.\n\n**Who else sees it** — Does the product layer in third-party analytics, ad tracking, or CRM tools that see your queries? Aethyro doesn''t. Just you and Anthropic''s API.\n\n**"We never sell your data"** — This is baseline, not a feature. Anyone not selling your data is meeting the floor, not doing something impressive. Push for specifics.\n\nThe short version: **read the privacy policy, not just the marketing page.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ Quick Shots\n\n- **Don''t start a new conversation for every question.** Claude has context — use it. Keep a running conversation for a project rather than starting fresh each time.\n\n- **Give it a role when the task is specialized.** "As a senior security engineer, review this code for vulnerabilities" gets better output than "review this code."\n\n- **Paste the actual thing.** Don''t describe your email — paste the email. Don''t summarize the contract clause — paste the clause. Claude works on what you give it, not your description of it.\n\n- **Ask it to disagree with you.** Try: *"Here''s my plan. Tell me why it''s wrong."* Useful every time.\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ What We''re Building\n\nWe''re doing this in public.\n\nAethyro right now: Claude Opus 5 in your browser, 200 free credits on signup, credit packs that never expire. That''s it. Simple.\n\nNext up: file uploads (so you can paste an actual contract into the chat), conversation memory across sessions, and team sharing. We''re building in order of what''s actually useful, not what sounds impressive in a roadmap.\n\nIf there''s something you need that we don''t have yet, reply and tell me. I read every email.\n\n---\n\n## 👋 See You Next Issue\n\nThe Dispatch comes out every 1–2 weeks. No filler. If a week is slow in the AI world, we''ll skip rather than manufacture content.\n\nNext up: **how to write prompts that actually work** — the real patterns, not the generic "be specific and provide context" advice you''ve already read 50 times.\n\nIf you got something from this, forward it to one person. That''s the whole growth strategy.\n\n— The Aethyro team\n\n*p.s. The chat is free. 200 credits, no card. If you haven''t tried it yet → [aethyro.com/app/chat.html](https://aethyro.com/app/chat.html)*',
  false,
  '2026-09-24 09:00:00+00'
)
